-- title:
--   Residue ring at a uniformiser has absNorm many elements
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a number field (a field with the `NumberField` structure, so in particular a finite extension of $\mathbb{Q}$), let $v$ be a point of the height-one spectrum of the ring of integers $\mathcal{O}_K$, i.e. a nonzero prime ideal `v.asIdeal` of $\mathcal{O}_K$, and let $v.\text{adicCompletion}\,K$ be the completion of $K$ at the $v$-adic valuation, with valuation ring $\mathcal{O}_v = v.\text{adicCompletionIntegers}\,K$. Let $\varpi \in \mathcal{O}_v$ be an element whose image in the completion has valuation exactly $\mathrm{ofAdd}(-1)$ in the multiplicative value group $\mathbb{Z}^{\mathrm{mult}}_{\ge 0}$, that is, $\varpi$ is a uniformiser. The conclusion is the equality of natural numbers $$\#\bigl(\mathcal{O}_v / (\varpi)\bigr) = \mathrm{absNorm}(v.\mathrm{asIdeal}),$$ where the left-hand side is `Nat.card` of the quotient of $\mathcal{O}_v$ by the ideal generated by the singleton $\{\varpi\}$, and the right-hand side is the absolute ideal norm of the prime $v$, i.e. the cardinality of $\mathcal{O}_K / v.\mathrm{asIdeal}$ (interpreted as $0$ when the quotient is infinite, which does not occur here).
--
--   This is the standard identification of the residue ring of the complete local ring at a finite place with the residue field $\mathcal{O}_K/\mathfrak{p}_v$, so that the residue characteristic-counting constant $N(v)$ may be computed from the ideal norm. It is used in the local harmonic analysis on $\mathrm{GL}_2$ over the completions, where volumes of double cosets and orbital integrals are expressed in powers of the residue cardinality.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsDedekindDomain_HeightOneSpectrum_natCard_adicCompletionIntegers_quot_span_eq_absNorm.lean

